course: dictionary
lesson: 11936
title: Candied: sweet words and sweet food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from food, and their meaning is easy to see when you know the food. «Grandma made candied peel for the Christmas cake.» Candied peel is orange or lemon skin cooked in sugar syrup until it is sweet and soft, so candied means cooked in sugar syrup to make it sweet.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «At the fair, Sam bought a candied apple.» Fairs and sweet apples on sticks tell you candied apple is a toffee apple. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Candied can also be a rare word for words. «His candied compliments made the teacher suspicious.» Here candied means too sweet or flattering in what someone says. The clue is suspicious: people do not usually feel suspicious of kind words, unless the kind words are too much.
fact: Candied means cooked in sugar syrup to make it sweet.
fact: Candied peel, candied fruit and candied apples are all sweet foods made this way.
fact: A candied apple is another name for a toffee apple.
fact: Candied yams are eaten at Thanksgiving in the US.
fact: Sugar helps stop germs growing, so candied fruit can last a long time.
exercise: «Grandma made candied peel for the Christmas cake.» What does candied mean here? | Sour like a lemon | *Cooked in sugar syrup and sweet | Cold and frozen | Burnt black in the oven
exercise: «At the fair, Sam bought a candied apple.» What is a candied apple also called? | *A toffee apple | A dried apple slice | A baked apple pie | A green apple
exercise: «The candied fruit lasted for months in the jar.» Why did the fruit last so long? | It was kept in the bin | It was frozen solid | *Sugar stops germs growing | It was too sour for anyone to eat
test: «His candied compliments made the teacher suspicious.» What does candied mean in this sentence? | Cooked in sugar syrup | *Too sweet or flattering in words | Cold and icy | Fried in oil
test: At a US Thanksgiving dinner, there are candied yams. Which festival is this? | Halloween | *Thanksgiving | Bonfire Night | Easter
exam: Tom says a candied apple is a green apple picked from a tree. Who is right? | Tom is right, candied means picked | *Tom is wrong: a candied apple is a toffee apple, cooked in sugar syrup | Tom is right, it is a green apple | Tom is right, it is a dried apple slice
